| `scripts/child_env.py` | Builds the environment a Python child process starts with from the configured allowlist (`build_child_env`) and says whether a value carries a credential (`carries_credential`), so no spawn hands a child the parent's whole environment. | imported; check_X holds every spawn to it | [`child_env.names`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Defence-in-depth, not a sandbox. Stays stdlib-only and 3.6-safe, because the hook interpreter imports it. Pattern compilation syntax, recursion and overflow faults refuse the policy by key and label without pattern or compiler text. Regex execution time is not bounded here. The `child_env` row below is the feature this module carries. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md) | always |
